# Timestamped .env copies made by tooling (.env.bak-1787800265168 and friends).
# The bare `.env` rule above does not match them, so two such files carrying a
# real SESSION_SECRET were sitting untracked-but-committable in the working
# tree: one `git add -A` away from publishing the secret that signs every admin
# and customer session. Match every variant, and keep .env.example tracked.
.env.*
!.env.example
